    "body": "## Purpose\n\n`get_moe_wna16_block_config` tests the same condition twice in a single boolean expression:\n\n```python\nif (\n    num_m_blocks <= 16\n    and size_k % (block_size_k * 2) == 0\n    and size_k % (block_size_k * 2) == 0   # <- identical to the line above\n    and block_size_k <= 512\n    and num_blocks >= 512\n):\n```\n\nSince `X and X` is equivalent to `X`, the second term can never affect the result. This removes it.\n\nThe duplicate dates back to the original commit (#13321, `[Kernel] moe wna16 cuda kernel`) and was preserved verbatim by the yapf-to-ruff reformat (#26247), so it has always been redundant rather than being introduced by a refactor.\n\nI've kept this to the mechanical removal only. If the second term was meant to check a different quantity (for example `size_n` / `block_size_n`), that would be a behavior change and should be a separate PR from someone who knows the intended tuning heuristic. Happy to follow up if a maintainer confirms the intent.\n\n## Test Plan\n\nThe change is intended to be a strict no-op, so I verified equivalence by exhaustively comparing the function before and after across its parameter space. Both versions were extracted and executed side by side over the cartesian product of:\n\n- `use_moe_wna16_cuda`: True, False\n- `num_valid_tokens`: 1, 2, 7, 16, 64, 256, 1024, 4096\n- `size_k`: 64, 128, 256, 512, 1024, 2048, 4096, 7168, 8192\n- `size_n`: 64, 128, 256, 512, 1024, 2048, 4096, 8192\n- `num_experts`: 1, 8, 64, 128, 256\n- `group_size`: 32, 64, 128\n- `real_top_k`: 1, 2, 8\n- `block_size_m`: 16, 32, 64\n\n## Test Result\n\n155,520 cases compared, 0 mismatches in the returned `BLOCK_SIZE_N` / `BLOCK_SIZE_K`.\n\n```\nsanity: HEAD has the dup twice, working tree once\n\ncases: 155520   mismatches: 0\n```\n\n## AI assistance disclosure\n\nPer the [AI attribution policy](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/main/docs/contributing/README.md): this change was found and prepared with AI assistance (Claude). The duplicate was located by an AST scan for repeated operands within a single boolean expression, and the equivalence check above was run to confirm the no-op. The commit carries a `Co-authored-by: Claude` trailer. I reviewed the change and the test result before submitting.",
